@arc vance
who: vance
// Writer (command), from outlines.md section 7, "Gull". His card's needs: practical, so the practical replies get the
// warmer answer. He never swears, not even "blast". That Gull is Vance is only said in beat 5.

== beat 1
tone: light
hint: Cadet. Have you read this week's newsletter? Sit. Briefly.
mem: gull
learn: Someone called Gull writes the worst poems in the ship's newsletter. Commander Vance has opinions about the scansion.
them: Someone at the next table is reading Gull's poem aloud. About the treadmill. It is very bad.   [sigh]
them: "Oh treadmill, thou belt of endless toil." Thou. In this century. The metre is wrong in line two.
them: It should be ten beats. It's eleven. I've counted. Twice.
? choice
* You seem to know it quite well, Commander.   flavour:cheer mem:suspect
  them: I read everything in the newsletter. It is my duty. Carry on.   [nod]
* How would you fix line two?   flavour:practical mem:fixed
  them: Remove "endless". Toil is endless by nature. It's implied.
  + them: Remove "endless". Toil is endless by nature. Then it scans. You have a good ear, cadet. Noted.   [gesture]
* I quite like it.   flavour:share mem:likeit
  them: You do? Hm. Well. Taste is not covered by regulations.
them: Whoever Gull is, they should be stopped. Gently.

== beat 2
tone: light
where: gym
hint: Cadet. A favour. Not an order. You can count?
mem: board
learn: Commander Vance timed himself against Lindqvist's treadmill record, with you on the stopwatch.
them: Lindqvist has taken the top of the treadmill board. By six seconds. Six.   [sigh]
them: I'd like you to time me. Formally. Start on my word.
? choice
* Ready when you are, Commander.   flavour:practical mem:timed
  them: Thank you. Three, two, one. Mark.
  + them: Good. Precise, quick and on time. Three, two, one. Mark.   [nod]
* Shall I cheer?   flavour:cheer mem:cheered
  them: Quietly. Very quietly. Three, two, one. Mark.   [laugh]
* Is this about Lindqvist?   flavour:listen mem:lindqvist
  them: It is about procedure. And Lindqvist. Three, two, one. Mark.
them: Well? One second? Ahead by one second.
them: Adequate.   [nod]

== beat 3
tone: heartfelt
hint: Cadet. A word. Not about work. If you've a moment.
mem: messages
learn: Commander Vance has two messages from his father he hasn't opened. They haven't spoken since the academy.
them: Two messages from home. From my father. They've been waiting since Sowing. I haven't opened them.   [sigh]
them: At the academy I broke the rules. Badly. They nearly sent me home, and he was ashamed of me.
them: We haven't spoken since. One is probably "I'm still ashamed". I can't guess the other.
? choice
* I'll sit with you while you open them. Whenever you're ready.   flavour:practical mem:sitwith
  them: That is a very sensible plan. I'll think on it.
  + them: That is a very sensible plan. Thorough, kind and possible. I'll think on it. Thank you.   [nod]
* That must have been a long time to carry it.   flavour:listen mem:listened
  them: Twenty-two years. I've carried heavier. Not for longer.
* My family and I don't always talk either.   flavour:share mem:shared
  them: Then you know the silence. It gets a shape, after a while.
them: Carry on, cadet. And thank you. Noted, and meant.

== beat 4
tone: heartfelt
gapDays: 2
when: beat:vance.3
hint: Cadet. I've decided. Will you sit with me a minute?
mem: opened
learn: Commander Vance opened his father's message. His father followed his whole career and wants to see him at the next port.
them: I'm opening the first one. Now. While I have the nerve. Sit there, please.   [sigh]
them: He followed my whole career. Every posting. He wrote them all down. He wants to see me at the next port.
them: Regulation eleven, section two: leave at port is granted on request. I don't know why I said that.
? choice
* Request the leave, Commander.   flavour:practical mem:leave
  them: Yes. That's the next correct step. I'll do it today.
  + them: Yes. Request, approve, attend. In that order. I'll fill in the form today. Thank you.   [nod]
* Read it again. I'm not going anywhere.   flavour:listen mem:again
  them: Thank you. I'll read it twice. Then once more.
* He wrote them all down. Like your list of juniors.   flavour:share mem:likehim
  them: Like my list. I hadn't thought of that. Hm. I'm his son, after all.
them: As you were. No. Stay a minute longer. That's an order. Of sorts.

== beat 5
tone: resolution
where: calm
when: time:evening|night
hint: Cadet. Something for you. Not regulation.
mem: therule
flag: vance.gull
keepsake: his academy rowing pin, which he says he's "lending" you
learn: As a cadet, Vance took a shuttle out without leave to bring back a stranded cadet. He's written to his father. He is Gull.
them: The rule I broke. A training shuttle, out without leave. Another cadet was stranded on a test flight.   [sigh]
them: I brought them back. I was nearly thrown out. They're a captain now. I've written to my father.
them: Next week's newsletter has a poem by Gull. About a father. It's still terrible. It's mine.
? choice
* I knew it. The scansion gave you away.   flavour:cheer mem:knew
  them: It's eleven beats again. I left it. Some things should stay a little wrong.   [laugh]
* I'm proud of you. All of it.   flavour:share mem:proud
  them: Thank you. That is not a thing anyone says to an XO. I'll file it carefully.
* Your secret's safe. I'll tell no one.   flavour:practical mem:safe
  them: Good. Correct, discreet and loyal. Take this. My rowing pin. I'm lending it to you.
  + them: Correct, discreet and loyal. Take this. My rowing pin. Lending it. Indefinitely. That's a regulation term.   [nod]
them: Tell no one I'm Gull. That's an order. Of sorts.
